Modules
/ The learner pages, each module's start.md in its own os folder (Ingi; a new /system/… file lands where its folder
/ is, the app's own /system/ first, else the os's: decision 522), each written from the module catalog, never by hand (decision 411; the spec is
/ Documentation/v0.2/module-reference-generation.md): the module's description, then each action's description,
/ the steps of its examples, its properties (how a step says each, its type, whether it is required, its default,
/ what it changes) and what it returns.
/ Only the file, condition and loop modules' notes are tagged (with a golden page each), so only their pages are
/ written. The loop over %!app.module.list% comes when every module's notes are tagged.
- call goal Page module=%!app.module.file%
- call goal Page module=%!app.module.condition%
- call goal Page module=%!app.module.loop%

Page
/ One module's page, system/modules/<name>/start.md, then what its actions' notes and properties don't agree on.
- render template "/templates/module.template", write to %page%
- save %page% to "/system/modules/%module.Name%/start.md"
- foreach %module.Action%, call Unmatched action=%item%

Unmatched
/ What one action's notes and properties don't agree on: a notes line that names no property, a property that no
/ line names. The notes find them (action.Note.Warning); this writes each one.
- foreach %action.Note.Warning%, call Warn warning=%item%

Warn
- write %warning.Message% to "error" channel
